---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
---
<Base title="About" description="What Procurement Signal is and who it's for.">
  <div class="page narrow">
    <div class="page-head"><h1>Procurement news, with the signal turned up.</h1></div>
    <div class="prose-page">
      <p>{SITE.name} is an independent publication for procurement and sourcing leaders: CPOs, category managers, sourcing leads and the teams who support them.</p>
      <p>Procurement news is scattered across trade publications, government notices, commodity markets, press wires and analyst blogs. We track all of it, connect the dots across sources, and publish what matters with a clear answer to the question every procurement team asks: <em>what does this mean for me?</em></p>
      <h2>What we publish</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>News</strong>: significant developments, synthesized from multiple sources.</li>
        <li><strong>Signal Reports</strong>: data-driven pieces built from tariff schedules, government contract data, commodity prices and deal activity.</li>
        <li><strong>Analysis</strong>: weekly trend pieces on where the function is heading.</li>
        <li><strong>Trackers</strong>: living reference pages for tariffs, compliance deadlines and more.</li>
        <li><strong>Price trends by category</strong>: monthly price-pressure readings for 12 purchase categories, built from official producer price data.</li>
        <li><strong>Guides and glossary</strong>: in-depth reference guides and plain-English definitions for procurement and supply chain professionals.</li>
        <li><strong>Industry headlines</strong>: the day's procurement and supply chain headlines from the trade press and official notices, linked to their sources.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>How we work</h2>
      <p>Our newsroom uses AI-assisted research and drafting under published <a href="/editorial-standards/">editorial standards</a>. Every story links to its original sources. Editor: {SITE.editor}.</p>
      <p>{SITE.name} is a personal, independent project. It is not affiliated with, sponsored by, or written on behalf of any employer or procurement vendor.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
